<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Siyaj K'ak'</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">active 378</span> · Also known as Sihyaj K'ahk', Smoking Frog</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Siyaj K'ak' was a war leader linked to Teotihuacan whose arrival in the Maya lowlands in 378 CE marked the 'entrada'. Passing through El Perú-Waka', he reached Tikal on the day its king Chak Tok Ich'aak died, and installed a new dynasty there; inscriptions at Uaxactun and other cities record his authority.</p></div>
